  clock: 5  # 4fa0
  nonce: 4fa0  # 4fa0
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #309, merged as cfe6e0e6cc. Behavioural evidence, re-run\nagainst the MERGED tree (dev 69e541f119), not a proxy:\n\n  hypergumbo verify-claims fixtures/popen --claims claims-subprocess.yaml\n      -> rc 1 (was rc 0 / confirmed)          the filed repro, closed\n  hypergumbo verify-claims fixtures/popen_control ...\n      -> rc 1                                  control, unchanged\n  hypergumbo verify-claims fixtures/telnet --claims claims.yaml\n      -> rc 2                                  INV-buzab regression control holds\n  hypergumbo verify-claims fixtures/requests --claims claims.yaml\n      -> rc 2                                  regression control holds\n\n  hypergumbo io-boundaries fixtures/popen\n      -> subprocess: 1 call(s) [HIGH RISK]  subprocess.Popen (1)\n         reachable from: main (main.py:4)\n      previously: an empty boundary map\n\nFIX: `instantiates` added to tag_io_boundaries' call_types, plus a parity test\nasserting _CALL_SITE_EDGE_TYPES is a SUBSET of it — one-directional on purpose,\nsince the tagger is legitimately broader (imports, the FFI family) and that\ndirection can only downgrade confirmed to inconclusive.\n\nDIRECTION, measured on real repos and additive only: poetry total_io_edges\n504 -> 516 (fs_write +10, subprocess +2), httpx 11 -> 13 (fs_write +2); all\nother boundaries and external_potential unchanged. The deltas matched the\npre-fix classify_call prediction exactly, which was the control on the\ninstrument.\n\nDISCLOSED, not closed by this: urllib.request.Request is catalogued net_send\nthough constructing a Request sends nothing. That row was inert while\nconstructors went untagged and is now visible — a catalogue judgement to revisit\nin the row, not in the edge-type set. And the measured population is Python-only\nbecause JavaScript emits 666 instantiates edges on pretix of which zero reach an\nexternal dst (WI-jubag), NOT because other analyzers are safe."  # 4fa0
